WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:01.660
Speaker 1: Welcome to the show.

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:07.040
What a big news weekend and so many different
things happening, the Kyle Rittenhouse case

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:12.640
is the trial is into closing arguments and
the jury will be deliberating.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:15.440
We may have a verdict soon, we don't yet know.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:19.789
We're going to talk about the case related
to the killing of Ahmaud Arbery.

00:00:19.789 --> 00:00:22.119
There's wacky stuff going on there.

00:00:22.119 --> 00:00:23.390
So many different things.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:28.080
But one of the big pieces of news news elements,
I would even call it breaking at the very

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:33.710
end of last week and into the weekend is the
indictment of former Trump adviser Stephen

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:39.160
K. Bannon, who has indeed been indicted on
contempt for ignoring a subpoena from the

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:43.670
committee investigating the Jan. six Trump
riots and of course, wanting to know Steve

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:44.680
Bannon's role in that.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:48.260
Given all of the public statements that he
has made very logical person that they would

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:49.260
want to talk to.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:50.740
He ignored the subpoena.

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:51.780
He is indicted.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:56.489
He is reportedly surrendering to authorities
today and will be arraigned.

00:00:56.489 --> 00:01:03.370
This is a big deal, and it is yet another
Trump associate who has been indicted for

00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:05.290
different reasons, of course.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:09.829
New York Times reporting Bannon indicted on
contempt charges over houses Capitol riot

00:01:09.829 --> 00:01:11.090
inquiry.

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:16.249
Stephen K. Bannon, a former top aide to Donald
Trump, had refused to comply with subpoenas

00:01:16.249 --> 00:01:21.810
from the House Committee investigating the
January 6th attack on Congress.

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:26.229
Stephen came in and a one time senior aide
to Trump was indicted by a federal grand jury

00:01:26.229 --> 00:01:31.909
Friday, two counts of contempt of Congress
after his refusal to provide information to

00:01:31.909 --> 00:01:37.329
the House Committee investigating what you
and I and reasonable people around the world

00:01:37.329 --> 00:01:38.919
know of as the Trump riots.

00:01:38.919 --> 00:01:44.020
Bannon, who's 67 years old, declined last
month to comply with subpoenas from the committee

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:46.279
seeking testimony and documents.

00:01:46.279 --> 00:01:50.340
The House then voted to hold Mr. Bannon in
criminal contempt of Congress.

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:55.229
The House referred the matter to the U.S.
Attorney's Office for a decision on prosecution.

00:01:55.229 --> 00:02:00.159
Trump has directed former aides and advisers
to invoke immunity and refrain from turning

00:02:00.159 --> 00:02:01.419
over documents.

00:02:01.419 --> 00:02:05.880
A Justice Department spokesman said Bannon
was expected to turn himself into authorities

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:10.259
Monday today and make his first appearance
in Federal District Court in Washington later

00:02:10.259 --> 00:02:11.259
today.

00:02:11.259 --> 00:02:15.819
A lawyer for Bannon didn't respond to a request
for comment.

00:02:15.819 --> 00:02:21.319
This is going to be a really, really crazy
period of time.

00:02:21.319 --> 00:02:27.640
The Department of Justice putting out a statement
official statement about what they did.

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:30.069
Stephen K. Bannon indicted for contempt of
Congress.

00:02:30.069 --> 00:02:34.260
Two charges filed for failing to honor House
subpoena.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:39.579
Bannon indicted on two counts, which I already
told you one count involving his refusal to

00:02:39.579 --> 00:02:44.069
appear for a deposition, another involving
his refusal to produce documents.

00:02:44.069 --> 00:02:46.319
Remember that you can subpoena an individual.

00:02:46.319 --> 00:02:47.959
You can also subpoena documents.

00:02:47.959 --> 00:02:54.390
He refused to show up, and he refused to provide
the documents.

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:58.239
This I don't know that we really need to read
much more of the statement.

00:02:58.239 --> 00:03:04.459
We continue to see a growing number of Trump
associates that have been indicted.

00:03:04.459 --> 00:03:10.209
We now have Steve Bannon, Tom Barrack Elliott
Broidy, Michael Cohen, who is down to his

00:03:10.209 --> 00:03:13.219
last 10 days or so of his home confinement
sentence.

00:03:13.219 --> 00:03:14.219
Michael Flynn.

00:03:14.219 --> 00:03:16.190
We're going to hear from him later in today's
program.

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:26.329
Rick Gates, Paul Manafort, George Nader, George
Papadopoulos, Roger Stone and Allen Weisselberg.

00:03:26.329 --> 00:03:28.939
Quite a list of quite a cadre.

00:03:28.939 --> 00:03:32.420
I guess we would say of characters there.

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:37.549
And the question continues to be, is this
going to reach Donald Trump ever?

00:03:37.549 --> 00:03:39.909
I continue to believe it will not.

00:03:39.909 --> 00:03:49.019
I continue to believe that the worst case
scenario for Trump would be some kind of business

00:03:49.019 --> 00:03:50.069
problem.

00:03:50.069 --> 00:03:55.159
I don't believe this is ever going to reach
Donald Trump, as you will hear in my comments

00:03:55.159 --> 00:03:56.159
later on.

00:03:56.159 --> 00:04:02.590
It is now being alleged by one of Trump's
former press secretaries that he would hold

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:11.260
off the books meetings specifically to circumvent
records laws to prevent there being records

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:13.390
about some of his meetings.

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:18.769
And arguably, that is a criminal issue, but
I just continue to believe that it is not

00:04:18.769 --> 00:04:21.630
going to get to him, and it is not for lack
of deserving it.

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:28.310
It is because of the system and the political
forces that we have at play in the United

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:29.310
States.

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:31.480
So what is ultimately going to happen with
Steve Bannon?

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:32.480
We don't know yet.

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:37.660
The arraignment coming later today believed
to be and this could be.

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:45.790
There are now allegations being made that
there are subpoenas going out to Mark Meadows,

00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:52.550
Trump's then chief of staff, potentially to
people like Stephen Miller and others, if

00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:55.210
they will also attempt to.

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:57.630
That's the one other thing I wanted to mention.

00:04:57.630 --> 00:05:01.400
What Steve Bannon did is staying loyal to
Trump.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:07.580
As The New York Times reports, Trump directed
Bannon and others not to comply with these

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:13.190
requests for their physical presence and their
requests for documents to be turned over.

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:16.099
So Bannon is staying loyal to Trump now.

00:05:16.099 --> 00:05:17.680
Trump no longer has pardon power.

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:20.910
Remember, Trump pardoned a number of different
people.

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:23.240
Michael Flynn's one of them who we're going
to talk about later.

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:29.660
Trump doesn't have pardon power anymore, so
either there is a play that Trump will eventually

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:33.930
be president again and pardon them if they
stay loyal.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:35.150
That's a long shot.

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:39.639
It's not that it's impossible or implausible,
but it's a long game.

00:05:39.639 --> 00:05:43.319
You've got to wait years for to see if Trump
is even going to run and then see if he's

00:05:43.319 --> 00:05:46.530
going to be the nominee and then see if he's
going to win and then see if you'll pardon

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:47.530
me.

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:49.470
So that's a very long play.

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:54.910
The other part of it would be they just believe
ultimately they're going to get out unscathed,

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:56.380
and that remains to be seen.

00:05:56.380 --> 00:06:01.060
But we'll see what happens at the arraignment
today and what the next step is here.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:03.370
Maybe there is a timing out aspect.

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:08.009
Maybe Bannon thinks, OK, I'm going to get
indicted.

00:06:08.009 --> 00:06:14.039
But in the time that my case will be pending,
the committee will be done and I might get

00:06:14.039 --> 00:06:15.599
a slap on the wrist.

00:06:15.599 --> 00:06:17.169
Probably not a big deal.

00:06:17.169 --> 00:06:20.640
But I will have avoided providing testimony
or documents.

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:21.640
I don't know.

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:24.229
OK, I don't know what the legal strategy is,
but we're going to see very, very soon

